# A stream window's toolbar (WindowToolbar): ⌘ keys, gestures (a Desktop's), quality, refresh and the
# launcher. ⌘ is the window's own Capture shortcuts: off at first, on and named ("Keys to …") from its
# button, off again; the launcher's switch sets every open window. A harness window never has the
# keyboard, so the tap itself is not made here (SystemKeyTap: only while the window's picture has it).
wait apps 30
click 75 242
wait stream 15
expect streamWindows.0.toolbar contains sill.keys
expect streamWindows.0.toolbar contains sill.gestures
expect streamWindows.0.toolbar contains sill.launcher
expect streamWindows.0.keys == false
toolbar keys
expect streamWindows.0.keys == true
expect streamWindows.0.keysTitle contains Keys to
snap toolbar-keys-on.png all
toolbar keys
expect streamWindows.0.keys == false
expect streamWindows.0.keysTitle !contains Keys to
capture on
expect streamWindows.0.keys == true
capture off
expect streamWindows.0.keys == false
key esc
toolbar launcher
expect launcher.shown == true
